{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_0178MccmxV89SmCHiE4LZVo4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. The `inventory` service is complete and all v1 unit tests pass; v2 tests skip cleanly without `PG_DSN` (as designed) and compile against the real `store.NewPGStore` / `server.NewServerWithStore` API.\n\n## What I found and did\n\nThe proto, generated stubs, `main.go`, Makefile, Dockerfile, and migration SQL already existed, plus a v1-only in-memory `server.go`. The **v2 layer was missing entirely** — the pre-written `server_v2_test.go` imports `internal/store` with `store.NewPGStore(...)` and `server.NewServerWithStore(...)`, neither of which existed. I built that out without touching the test files.\n\n**New `internal/store` package** (behind a single `Store` interface, per the SPEC's two-backend design):\n- `store.go` — `Store` interface + sentinel errors (`ErrNotFound`, `ErrInsufficient`, `ErrConsumed`) + shared hold-ID/status helpers.\n- `mem.go` — `NewMemStore()`, the v1 in-memory backend (ported from the old server, mutex-serialized).\n- `pg.go` — `PGStore` / `NewPGStore(ctx, dsn)` using `pgxpool`. `Hold` takes a `SELECT … FOR UPDATE` row lock inside a transaction so concurrent holds serialize and never oversell (the v2 concurrency contract); `Commit`/`Release` lock the hold row. `SetStock` upserts, preserving `sold`/`held`.\n\n**Refactored `server.go`** — `Server` now delegates to a `Store`. `NewServer()` uses the in-memory backend; added `NewServerWithStore(Store)`. Request-shape validation stays in the server (→ `InvalidArgument`); a `mapErr` helper maps store sentinels to `NotFound` / `FailedPrecondition`.\n\n**`main.go`** — selects the Postgres backend when `PG_DSN` is set, falls back to in-memory otherwise (matches the SPEC's `connection_env: PG_DSN`).\n\n**`go.mod`/`go.sum`** — `go mod tidy` added `github.com/jackc/pgx/v5`; no stray cross-service requires (`dependent_interface` is empty).\n\n## Verification\n- `go generate ./...` (protoc regen), `go build ./...`, `go vet ./...` — all clean.\n- `go test ./...` — server package passes; store/api/cmd have no test files.\n\nNote: I ran with `GOWORK=off` because this sandbox's root `go.work` references sibling services (booking, cancellation, payment, tests/integration) that aren't present here — that's a sandbox artifact, not something to fix. `make build`/`make test` will use the workspace normally in the full repo. The Dockerfile is unchanged and correct for a leaf service (service-dir build context, distroless, exposes 50051/8080)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":131,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1140,"cache_read_input_tokens":54247,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1140},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d05fd576-efd5-43de-be9a-3bd55105bdb9","uuid":"e6e96196-1aaa-4a8b-8e27-1af179566287","request_id":"req_011Cbnm179sMAhKX4XkShquw"}
